      "section": "S1",
      "question_number": 58,
      "question_text": "58 The relative tendency for metals to form positive ions in solution can be measured using the following apparatus: voltmeter V inert conductor _ + metal 1 metal 2 1 mol dm–3 solution 1 mol dm–3 solution of metal 1 ions of metal 2 ions Electrons can pass from metal 1 to metal 2 via the external circuit. The difference in the tendency of the metals to form positive ions is given by the reading on the voltmeter. The higher the reading on the voltmeter the greater the difference in the tendency of the pair of metals to form positive ions. Results from three experiments are given in the following table. experiment metal 1 metal 2 reading on voltmeter / V 1 P Q +0.62 2 S Q +0.30 3 S R +1.24 Using the information in the table, what is the order of reactivity of the four metals P, Q, R and S, from most reactive to least reactive?",
